5.16.1 includes two parts: Part 1: The trigger condition for SN gap report (marked with yellow); Part 2: How to set the PDCP SN gap report (marked with blue). For Part 1, when discussing the trigger condition, the SDU should satisfy the following three conditions: PDCP SDU(s) are discarded; Discarded may be caused by any of the following three cases: 1) due to its own discardTimer expiry; 2) due to the discardTimer expiry of SDU belonging to the same PDU Set; 3) confirmed by PDCP status report. There is at least one stored PDCP SDU(s) which is associated with a COUNT value larger than the COUNT value associated to the discarded PDCP SDU(s); The discarded PDCP SDU(s) have not been submitted by RLC to lower layers. For example, in the following figure, PDCP SDU1/2/3 all belongs to PDU Set 1, the PDCP SDU1 has been delivered to MAC by RLC, PDCP SDU2 has been delivered to RLC but has not been delivered to MAC, and PDCP SDU3 is still in PDCP. At T4, the discardTimer of PDCP SDU1 expiries. Assuming pdu-SetDiscard is configured for PDU Set 1, all of PDCP SDU1/2/3 should be discarded at the same time. But considering PDCP SDU1 has been delivered to MAC, it should not trigger SN gap report. If there is other PDCP SDUs which associated COUNT larger than the COUNT of PDCP SDU3, PDCP SDU2 and PDCP SDU3 can trigger SN gap report. Figure-1 Illustration of the SN gap report trigger Observation 1: It is possible that more than one PDCP SDUs are discarded simultaneously, but only partial of them can trigger PDCP SN gap report according to the current specification. In case of more than one PDCP SDUs are discarded simultaneously, but only partial of them trigger PDCP SN gap report, it should further discuss whether the COUNT of the discarded PDCP SDU which with COUNT value smaller than the COUNT value of PDCP SDU which trigger the PDCP SN gap but have been delivered by RLC to lower layers should be included in the PDCP SN gap or not. Take Figure-1 as example, what we need to discuss is that whether the COUNT of PDCP SDU1 should be included in the PDCP SN gap report. Proposal 1: Suggest RAN2 to discuss whether the discarded PDCP SDU(s) which have been delivered by RLC to lower layers should be included in the PDCP SN gap report or not.
